  "label": "User projected onto the text and visual elements expressing hateful rhetoric",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the meme's textual and visual components that express extreme hatred and conspiracy theories. The text 'i'm here to claim the rights of husband' and 'i hate all freemasons and christians' directly address the viewer ('you', 'i') and project the user's identity onto the hateful stance. The visual elements (knight, woman, flag) serve as the medium through which this projection is realized, making the user feel personally implicated in or aligned with the hateful message.",
